<title>USA: SEC drops probe of Denver air engineers -- firms.</title>
<headline>SEC drops probe of Denver air engineers -- firms.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Commission staff on Friday notified two engineering firms that the SEC is closing its probe of Denver International Airport bond offerings without seeking fraud charges against them.</p>
<p>Richard Parry, vice president of law for Morrison Knudsen Corp said: &quot;We received official notice today from the central regional office of SEC that they are terminating their formal investigation of the Denver Airport matter without bringing (action against the firm).</p>
<p>&quot;This was the appropriate result. We expected it all the time.&quot;</p>
